#!/bin/sh
# Run a Django management command for one ApplyForge release, as the `applyforge`
# user, with exactly the service's production environment - without ever loading
# the secrets into an administrator's shell. Milestone 8.4c; see deploy/README.md.
#
# Usage (as root):
#   applyforge-manage <release-dir> <manage.py arguments...>
# Examples:
#   applyforge-manage /srv/applyforge/releases/<commit> check --deploy
#   applyforge-manage /srv/applyforge/releases/<commit> migrate --plan
#   applyforge-manage /srv/applyforge/releases/<commit> collectstatic --noinput
#
# The release directory is explicit (not `current`) so a NEW release can be
# checked, migrated and have its static files collected before traffic is
# switched to it. deploy/preflight.py runs first; the command does not run if it fails.
#
# Sandbox: same environment file, dotenv guard and network restriction
# (localhost only) as the service. Writable: STATIC_ROOT (collectstatic) and
# MEDIA_ROOT only.
set -eu

ENV_FILE=/etc/applyforge/applyforge.env
SERVICE_USER=applyforge
WRITABLE="/var/lib/applyforge/static /var/lib/applyforge/media"

if [ "$#" -lt 2 ]; then
    echo "usage: $0 <release-dir> <manage.py arguments...>" >&2
    exit 2
fi
if [ "$(id -u)" -ne 0 ]; then
    echo "$0: run as root (sudo); the command itself runs as $SERVICE_USER." >&2
    exit 2
fi

RELEASE=$(readlink -f -- "$1")
shift
case "$RELEASE" in
    /srv/applyforge/releases/*) ;;
    *) echo "$0: release must be under /srv/applyforge/releases/" >&2; exit 2 ;;
esac
PYTHON="$RELEASE/.venv/bin/python"
if [ ! -x "$PYTHON" ] || [ ! -f "$RELEASE/backend/manage.py" ] || [ ! -f "$RELEASE/deploy/preflight.py" ]; then
    echo "$0: $RELEASE is not a complete release (backend/, deploy/, .venv/)." >&2
    exit 2
fi
if [ ! -f "$ENV_FILE" ]; then
    echo "$0: $ENV_FILE is missing." >&2
    exit 2
fi

run() {
    systemd-run --quiet --pipe --wait --collect --service-type=exec \
        --uid="$SERVICE_USER" --gid="$SERVICE_USER" \
        -p WorkingDirectory="$RELEASE/backend" \
        -p Environment=APPLYFORGE_DOTENV=/nonexistent/applyforge-no-dotenv \
        -p Environment=PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 \
        -p Environment=PYTHONUNBUFFERED=1 \
        -p EnvironmentFile="$ENV_FILE" \
        -p UMask=0022 \
        -p NoNewPrivileges=yes \
        -p PrivateTmp=yes \
        -p ProtectHome=yes \
        -p ProtectSystem=strict \
        -p ReadWritePaths="$WRITABLE" \
        -p IPAddressAllow=localhost \
        -p IPAddressDeny=any \
        "$PYTHON" "$@"
}

run "$RELEASE/deploy/preflight.py"
run "$RELEASE/backend/manage.py" "$@"
